# LF everywhere, including in the working tree on Windows. This branch is the pristine
# upstream baseline, compared byte-for-byte against a VS Code checkout, so a worktree that
# checked out CRLF would make every file here look modified and silently disable both the
# divergence audit and the copy script's protection rule.
#
# This is the one file on `vendor` the copy script does not produce. It has to be here
# rather than only on `main`, because Git reads attributes from the branch being checked
# out, and a fresh worktree on `vendor` has no other source of them.
* text=auto eol=lf
